  "semantics": {
    "guards": "Player inactive bit1 or escape-triggered game-event bit3 skips contact before coordinate work. Other player/event bits do not gate this prefix. Fire and the unrelated periodic-security countdown are not read by this contact handler.",
    "rectangle": "Descriptor WORD XY plus state offsets, descriptor X+16 and Y+16 except identities20/21 Y+32; player WORD XY+16. All additions/subtractions wrap modulo65536; signed-negative magnitudes retain8000. Require unsigned X magnitude below18 AND Y below32. No Manhattan sum. Far releases node holds, retaining movement-inhibit and escape-card values. Near clears movement inhibition before checking cards.",
    "card_choices": "Exact descriptor identities18/19/20/21 require held BYTE IDs48/49/50/55 and select seen bits0/1/2/3. Unknown descriptor identity reaching this role skips all four checks and shares bit0, accepting every held ID in the controlled tests. Existing descriptor field labels and pointer forms remain unchanged.",
    "escape_card_producer": "Within contact handling, only in-range descriptor21 clears then recomputes event bit4. Wrong card clears it before damage; far/inactive/escape-triggered paths retain its previous value. This is a producer/consumer contract, not complete writer or alias closure.",
    "authorization": "BSET selected seen bit first. Only a previously clear bit requests audio0118 then increments count BYTE modulo256. Already-seen authorization still holds the chain without increment/feedback. Count is independent stored state, not recomputed from bits. Two unknown descriptors share bit0 and continue after the real audio call, incrementing once.",
    "attachment_hold": "Walk root then each non-NULL attachment; BSET or BCLR node mode bit0 only. Every other node byte, including WORD frame index/phase, survives. No frame restart is performed by this call. Original four chains have1/1/2/2 states, six distinct non-NULL nodes. Readable nodes and finite chains are inputs; arbitrary replacements/cycles/lifetimes are not proved.",
    "rejection": "Set movement inhibition FF and subtract10 from HP low BYTE. Wrapped results1..127 survive and update only that byte. Results0 or128..255 branch to defeat before storing the computed byte. Surviving contact draws health, requests shared0102 feedback and returns from the whole descriptor scan.",
    "defeat": "Use the existing animated defeat state, set its geometry, clear node clock and hold-header bit, mark player inactive and exchange active/saved states through the original helper. Reload exit delay70, clear whole HP WORD, draw health and queue outcomes, then return from the whole scan. Unlike the separately documented static-state failure route, this known incoming node is non-NULL.",
    "shared_feedback": "Three observed direct callers remain: contact survivor802A, missing-ID defeat8748 and collect_world_object_item4B17E. Name start_id_failure_or_item_handoff_audio reflects all three rather than assigning a damage-only sound purpose. The request value is0102; DMA/audibility are not inferred.",
    "escape_consumer": "At977E require event bit4 and decoded D0 low WORD236; no selected-card or checkpoint-count recheck. Set escape event bit3, install player escape geometry and clear its node, clear four initializer-relative bytes EBD/EC9/ED5/EE1, clear feedback event bit7, request audio mode1 with A6 saved/restored, then tail-call the existing outcome/inhibition helper. Because escape bit3 is already set, that helper retains inherited exit delay, including0/70/255."
  },
